    <!-- https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/Reference -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/Reference">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The taxonomy of references includes the reference tables found in the advisory leaflet DWA-M 150.

DWA-M 150 categorizes reference tables by type of data. Examples are:
- Reference Table 105: Material Types (Class/Subclass: Reference/Material)
- Reference Table 202: Condition Assessment Coding Systems (Reference/CodingSystem)

Each subclass refers to a specific reference table in DWA-M 150, implied with the equivalentTo axiom &quot;hasReferenceTable value &quot;[RefTableNumber]&quot;&quot;.

The different types found within a reference table are then listed as subclasses of the aforementioned subclass.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/ReferenceReport -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/ReferenceReport">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/Reference"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/Report -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto/Report">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The taxonomy of reports includes inspection and condition reports for a sewage system, according to the structure of the advisory leaflet DWA-M 150.

It is recommended to create individuals for inspection reports with the template:

` Inspection[PipeSectionDesignation]_[Date] `;
` Inspection[HG001]_[HI003] ` for Pipe Section: Inspection reports;
` Inspection[KG001]_[KI003] ` for Node: Inspection reports.

It is recommended to create individuals for condition reports within an inspection with the template:

` Condition[PipeSectionDesignation]_[Stationing(ConditionReport)]_[Code] `;
` Condition[HG001]_[HZ001]_[HZ002] ` for Pipe Section: Condition reports;
` Condition[HG001]_[KZ001]_[KZ002] ` for Node: Condition reports.

According to the DWA-M 150, the coding systems that can be applied here are:
- DIN EN 13508-2
- DWA 149-2
- DWA ATV-M 143
- ISYBAU2001
- ISYBAU1996</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


